Executive Summary

On 8 June 2026, Sam Altman and Jakub Pachocki published Built to benefit everyone: our plan, an essay promising that artificial intelligence will broaden power, preserve human judgment, remain subject to public coordination, distribute prosperity, avoid total automation and eventually provide every person on Earth with a personal AGI.

On the same calendar date, OpenAI separately announced that it had recently submitted a confidential draft S-1, preserving its option to become a publicly traded company. Three months earlier, OpenAI had closed a funding round containing $122 billion in committed capital at an $852 billion post-money valuation. 

This does not reveal a hidden conspiracy.

It reveals a business.

OpenAI itself says its commercial system now includes subscriptions, usage-priced APIs, commerce, advertising and compute. It reported annualised revenue rising from $2 billion in 2023 to more than $20 billion in 2025 and describes a compounding flywheel in which more compute produces stronger models, stronger models create more usage, usage generates revenue, and revenue finances more infrastructure. 

The actual operating equation is therefore:

\text{Compute}
\rightarrow
\text{Capability}
\rightarrow
\text{Usage}
\rightarrow
\text{Revenue}
\rightarrow
\text{More compute}

The public essay adds:

\text{More usage}
\rightarrow
\text{Power broadly distributed}

But that second implication does not follow.

Distributing access to a privately governed service is not the same as distributing ownership, infrastructure, voting rights, model control or economic upside. A billion customers do not collectively own the supermarket merely because every one of them may enter it.

OpenAI has built a highly valuable product and wants substantially more people to use it. That is coherent. What is incoherent is presenting mass consumption of that product as though it were equivalent to democratic control of the technology.

The company is not proposing that everyone own AGI.

It is proposing that everyone have an OpenAI account.

